WEBVTT

01:45.313 --> 01:46.981
Is that so?

01:49.067 --> 01:51.569
You have a theme to work on now?

01:53.446 --> 01:55.490
<i>He knows what to work on now?</i>

01:56.658 --> 01:57.992
<i>Baki Hanma...</i>

01:58.910 --> 02:01.496
<i>Whether you've got the theme or not.</i>

02:02.080 --> 02:04.415
<i>Whether you're asleep or awake.</i>

02:06.167 --> 02:10.130
<i>It doesn't change the fact
you're a giant monster to me!</i>

02:11.422 --> 02:12.632
<i>Well, then.</i>

02:14.134 --> 02:15.885
<i>Guess it's time to get to it.</i>

02:16.970 --> 02:18.888
<i>Time to slay the monster.</i>

02:19.973 --> 02:23.101
<i>I say, "slay the monster,"</i>

02:23.184 --> 02:27.397
<i>but this ain't martial arts I'm doing.</i>

02:27.480 --> 02:30.900
<i>I'm making it look like
I'll throw an uppercut,</i>

02:30.984 --> 02:35.613
<i>and in reality,
I'm actually throwing an uppercut.</i>

02:36.990 --> 02:40.618
<i>For a super-top-class
master martial artist like Baki,</i>

02:40.702 --> 02:43.913
<i>I bet this fight is so boring
that it would make him yawn.</i>

02:47.500 --> 02:49.669
<i>Sorry, Baki.</i>

02:50.795 --> 02:51.671
<i>But ya know...</i>

02:52.839 --> 02:55.675
<i>But ya know, Baki, I hope you understand.</i>

02:57.510 --> 03:00.054
<i>This here fight of ours,</i>

03:00.138 --> 03:03.433
<i>is different from fights
between master martial artists like you.</i>

03:03.516 --> 03:06.186
<i>It's not about beating or being beaten.</i>

03:13.818 --> 03:16.571
<i>The fight between us</i>

03:16.654 --> 03:21.951
<i>will only end
when one of us admits defeat.</i>

03:28.291 --> 03:29.876
<i>There are times,</i>

03:29.959 --> 03:33.171
<i>even when you're standing
over your fallen opponent,</i>

03:33.922 --> 03:36.090
<i>when you can still lose.</i>

03:40.678 --> 03:45.099
<i>That's what it means to settle our fight.</i>

03:45.683 --> 03:48.853
Baki, don't say a thing and--

03:50.438 --> 03:54.859
<i>Chiharu, thank you.
I'm honored to learn from you.</i>

03:55.902 --> 03:59.614
Stretching before a fight
is so unlike you.

04:02.408 --> 04:05.411
I'll show you the Chiharu Shiba.

04:05.495 --> 04:06.955
Me?

04:07.455 --> 04:08.456
Is that okay?

04:09.415 --> 04:11.876
I want to fight like Chiharu Shiba.

04:11.960 --> 04:15.421
Now, now, now.

04:15.505 --> 04:17.840
Don't go pulling my leg.

04:17.924 --> 04:20.635
If I were you,

04:21.302 --> 04:23.888
I'd fight like Baki Hanma.

04:24.472 --> 04:26.349
I'd like to do that too.

04:27.016 --> 04:28.935
That would be easiest for me.

04:29.644 --> 04:30.478
But...

04:31.437 --> 04:35.483
But that wouldn't settle this,
no matter how many times I defeat you.

04:38.569 --> 04:43.408
Until you're killed... no, even after
you're dead, you'd still put up a fight.

04:43.491 --> 04:44.867
You think you can...

04:45.493 --> 04:47.370
You punk,

04:47.453 --> 04:50.415
you fuckin' think you can fight like me?!

04:52.041 --> 04:52.917
Yeah, I can.

04:53.584 --> 04:55.336
<i>You bastard...</i>

04:58.506 --> 05:00.425
<i>I can, Chiharu.</i>

05:02.093 --> 05:03.177
<i>You bet I can.</i>

05:04.512 --> 05:05.680
<i>Why, you ask?</i>

05:07.515 --> 05:09.100
<i>Chiharu, you see...</i>

05:11.352 --> 05:12.854
<i>I admire you.</i>

05:16.733 --> 05:17.692
Baki...

05:18.901 --> 05:19.736
See?

05:21.154 --> 05:23.573
Bet you didn't expect me
to be so good at it.

05:27.410 --> 05:28.578
It's the "Chiharu way."

05:30.496 --> 05:31.956
<i>Don't hold back on the onset.</i>

05:32.498 --> 05:34.834
<i>Don't wait until the arm
is fully stretched out.</i>

05:35.668 --> 05:37.337
<i>At the max point of impact,</i>

05:38.046 --> 05:39.922
<i>make contact with absolute precision.</i>

05:41.758 --> 05:44.594
<i>That's the so-called, "Chiharu way."</i>

05:45.803 --> 05:49.098
<i>A constitution that's ordinary,
but a psyche like steel.</i>

05:49.807 --> 05:53.186
<i>But Chiharu's "steel"
was starting to crack.</i>

05:56.439 --> 05:58.941
An average black belt
doesn't even compare to you.

06:00.276 --> 06:02.195
Through sheer fighting spirit...

06:02.862 --> 06:06.657
Just on feeling alone, you can climb
to great heights, to a new state of mind.

06:07.200 --> 06:09.660
As if you're lifting yourself up
all on your own.

06:10.411 --> 06:12.705
Still, the sacrifice was worth it.

06:14.040 --> 06:18.669
In exchange for the damage to my face,
I've taken your right hand and left leg.

06:19.420 --> 06:21.964
Chiharu, why don't we stop this?

06:22.507 --> 06:25.093
There's no need to destroy
your remaining left hand.

06:25.760 --> 06:27.220
Baki.

06:27.929 --> 06:31.808
You said you were gonna show me
the Chiharu Shiba.

06:32.475 --> 06:36.020
You want to show me
the Chiharu way, isn't that right?

06:37.230 --> 06:38.981
Your final answer...

06:40.983 --> 06:42.610
Show me.

06:48.199 --> 06:51.119
<i>Taking hits with one's weakest point
is the Chiharu way.</i>

06:51.202 --> 06:54.414
You know where I'm aiming for, don't you?

06:54.956 --> 06:56.874
Try and take it!

06:58.751 --> 07:01.379
<i>The both of them had the other...</i>

07:03.506 --> 07:05.007
<i>on the ropes.</i>

07:05.675 --> 07:07.969
Don't miss, Chiharu.

07:09.554 --> 07:11.389
This ain't my first rodeo.

07:12.807 --> 07:15.268
<i>It isn't exposing one's weakness.</i>

07:16.602 --> 07:20.648
<i>In fact, it's the Chiharu Shiba way
to use that weakness as a weapon.</i>

07:22.525 --> 07:27.029
<i>Your face, where soft nose,
lips and cheeks coexist,</i>

07:28.281 --> 07:31.159
<i>is being attacked by a hard, tough fist.</i>

07:31.826 --> 07:33.828
<i>Then give them what they want.</i>

07:33.911 --> 07:36.038
<i>Meet the strong point
with your weak point.</i>

07:36.747 --> 07:39.417
<i>Then crush their confidence.</i>

07:40.710 --> 07:42.128
<i>Your injured right arm</i>

07:42.628 --> 07:46.048
<i>is targeted by a kick
trained to be hard as steel.</i>

07:47.175 --> 07:48.551
<i>Then welcome it.</i>

07:49.427 --> 07:51.804
<i>Let them smash into it
until they are satisfied.</i>

07:51.888 --> 07:55.266
<i>Transforming weak points into weapons
is the Chiharu Shiba way.</i>

07:56.976 --> 08:01.272
<i>That Chiharu way now had
Chiharu Shiba himself on the ropes.</i>

08:02.273 --> 08:03.191
You lie.

08:04.400 --> 08:07.695
Chiharu Shiba has never once
poked someone's eyes out.

08:09.530 --> 08:11.908
Aiming for vital spots
is the martial arts way.

08:13.159 --> 08:16.370
<i>Therefore, the Chiharu way
is the exact opposite.</i>

08:16.996 --> 08:19.373
<i>Your way isn't a martial art.</i>

08:20.666 --> 08:22.335
There's no way you could do that.

08:24.295 --> 08:27.423
<i>Poking your fingers into the eyeballs,
the ultimate vital spot.</i>

08:27.924 --> 08:31.469
<i>That's something that must never occur
in Chiharu Shiba's life.</i>

08:32.845 --> 08:35.723
Chiharu, poke good and straight.

08:37.642 --> 08:39.477
Eye-poking is a high-level skill.

08:40.561 --> 08:42.230
<i>Your opponent moves at will,</i>

08:42.313 --> 08:45.233
<i>yet your target is a mere
two or three centimeters in size.</i>

08:45.316 --> 08:49.237
<i>It's as difficult as simultaneously
catching two flies buzzing in the air.</i>

08:50.780 --> 08:52.740
<i>There's no way you could ever do it.</i>

08:53.574 --> 08:56.702
I'll poke my eyes into your two fingers.

08:58.120 --> 09:00.540
All you gotta do
is thrust your arm out straight.

09:01.874 --> 09:05.461
I'll twist your fingers with my eyeballs.

09:06.087 --> 09:08.506
There's no takin' it back.

09:08.589 --> 09:10.383
The shame you've caused...

09:10.466 --> 09:12.635
All the big talk...

09:12.718 --> 09:15.721
We have no choice but to move forward.

09:15.805 --> 09:18.099
Our only path now is to do this.

09:29.193 --> 09:32.613
<i>Later, Chiharu Shiba
recounted what happened.</i>

09:33.864 --> 09:36.993
<i>He said he never had any intention
of crushing Baki's eyes.</i>

09:38.077 --> 09:41.539
<i>He was going to make a fist
just before he struck.</i>

09:42.790 --> 09:47.545
<i>But in reality,
was there even enough time for that?</i>

09:50.881 --> 09:52.049
<i>Ultimate move: unleashed.</i>

09:52.633 --> 09:56.304
<i>Shall we call this the "Cockroach Dash"?</i>

10:11.944 --> 10:14.947
So, what will you do?

10:15.740 --> 10:18.951
Since you're still inexperienced,
this will surely happen to you.

10:19.535 --> 10:22.455
When you're struck
and your brain is shaken,

10:22.538 --> 10:24.957
it cannot be stopped with half measures.

10:25.541 --> 10:31.464
If you just wait, then it can take five
or even ten minutes to recover.

10:32.214 --> 10:34.467
You are at the mercy of your opponent.

10:34.550 --> 10:35.968
So, what will you do?

10:37.637 --> 10:39.180
It goes without saying,

10:39.263 --> 10:42.016
if you cannot wait,
then you go and meet it.

10:43.893 --> 10:45.978
Do you understand, Retsu?

10:48.606 --> 10:52.902
To stop something from shaking,
you must shake with it.

10:52.985 --> 10:54.820
You meet it yourself.

10:58.741 --> 11:00.451
<i>Open your ears.</i>

11:01.202 --> 11:02.703
<i>Listen to your brain.</i>

11:04.038 --> 11:06.499
<i>Pay attention to its shaking.</i>

11:07.708 --> 11:11.629
<i>What is the right timing to meet you?</i>

11:12.713 --> 11:13.881
<i>If you screw this up,</i>

11:14.590 --> 11:16.133
<i>you'll never stand up again.</i>

11:21.263 --> 11:23.474
<i>Meet the damage!</i>

11:32.566 --> 11:35.653
<i>I welcome you, damage.</i>

11:37.196 --> 11:39.949
<i>He stood up? Fine.</i>

11:42.743 --> 11:45.413
<i>That's fine. That's fine too.</i>

11:46.747 --> 11:48.124
<i>It doesn't change anything.</i>

12:01.637 --> 12:05.349
Isn't this where you give me advice?

12:06.517 --> 12:08.853
I only know about boxing.

12:08.936 --> 12:11.564
I can't advise you
on something that's not boxing.

12:12.273 --> 12:16.527
This is pathetic, but I don't even know
what the heck's going on in the ring.

12:17.153 --> 12:20.364
I have no idea how you're able to fight,
how you're dodging,

12:20.448 --> 12:23.409
or even how you got back up.

12:26.912 --> 12:27.830
They're the same.

12:30.666 --> 12:32.710
No matter what kind of moves I use,

12:33.294 --> 12:35.838
I am still only using my two fists.

12:36.422 --> 12:39.925
That is the Western kung fu
you know so well, boxing.

12:43.220 --> 12:46.348
It's ridiculous that a second
is getting advice from his boxer.

12:47.266 --> 12:48.434
Please give me advice!

12:48.934 --> 12:49.769
Huh?

12:50.644 --> 12:54.857
Give it everything you've...

12:54.940 --> 12:56.108
Watch out!

12:58.110 --> 12:59.361
<i>That is enough.</i>

12:59.987 --> 13:01.614
<i>Use everything that I've got.</i>

13:02.198 --> 13:03.449
<i>That is accurate advice.</i>

13:04.700 --> 13:07.453
<i>I will follow it.
Accept it with gratitude.</i>

13:08.829 --> 13:12.374
<i>Only the lazy think they've already used
everything they've got.</i>

13:14.043 --> 13:15.127
<i>Once more.</i>

13:16.003 --> 13:17.379
<i>In fact, now's the time</i>

13:18.422 --> 13:19.882
<i>to use everything I have</i>

13:21.300 --> 13:22.802
<i>as if it's the first time!</i>

13:26.722 --> 13:27.640
<i>That is...</i>

13:30.392 --> 13:32.102
<i>how to repay my coach!</i>

13:41.612 --> 13:42.530
At last.

13:43.197 --> 13:45.866
This is starting to look more like boxing.

13:47.910 --> 13:50.037
Whoa! Joe is down!

13:50.621 --> 13:52.623
Cruiser's been knocked down!

13:59.630 --> 14:01.006
Seriously?!

14:01.674 --> 14:05.052
My own boxer brought Joe to his knees!

14:08.639 --> 14:12.560
<i>Now that Joe has gotten back up</i>,

14:12.643 --> 14:13.894
<i>that's when...</i>

14:14.895 --> 14:16.063
Fight!

14:16.146 --> 14:19.191
<i>...boxing goes beyond the realm of sports.</i>

14:19.817 --> 14:21.610
<i>You can't call it a game anymore.</i>

14:25.197 --> 14:27.366
There it is! He's covering his eyes!

14:55.394 --> 14:57.313
You certainly are sweating a lot.

14:59.773 --> 15:00.608
<i>How come?</i>

15:01.609 --> 15:05.613
The genius fighter Retsu,
you can't even land a single punch.

15:06.655 --> 15:10.618
Why can't you defeat me, an old man
who's only using jumping techniques?

15:10.701 --> 15:11.827
I haven't lost!

15:13.120 --> 15:14.538
But you can't win either.

15:23.589 --> 15:24.798
Do you understand?

15:26.926 --> 15:29.094
When someone attacks from above,

15:29.178 --> 15:31.430
all you can do is defend against them.

15:36.185 --> 15:38.687
He's coming from overhead!
And he's spinning!

15:38.771 --> 15:42.316
Watch out for a wounded Joe.

15:46.654 --> 15:48.948
Boxing is a fight to the death.

15:57.039 --> 15:57.957
Okay, Joe?

15:58.916 --> 16:00.209
Okay.

16:00.793 --> 16:01.669
Fight!

16:01.752 --> 16:04.213
From here on, it's a fight to the death.

16:04.922 --> 16:08.717
<i>The energy that Joe has left
is on the verge of flickering out.</i>

16:08.801 --> 16:09.718
<i>Now's my chance!</i>

16:11.595 --> 16:12.471
<i>That hit home.</i>

16:13.347 --> 16:15.224
<i>That too. That too.</i>

16:15.891 --> 16:17.977
<i>The end... it's close.</i>

16:20.312 --> 16:21.146
Look!

16:21.230 --> 16:22.481
Joe's not dead yet!

16:24.400 --> 16:25.234
<i>Danger!</i>

16:26.068 --> 16:27.236
<i>Into the air!</i>

16:28.862 --> 16:30.239
He hit him in the air!

16:34.451 --> 16:37.913
<i>What incredible perseverance.</i>

16:38.622 --> 16:42.751
<i>His body must have taken serious damage!</i>

16:53.595 --> 16:57.016
<i>So this... this is Smoking Joe!</i>

16:57.599 --> 16:59.268
<i>That's right.</i>

16:59.351 --> 17:02.354
<i>This guy, he's Smoking Joe, dammit!</i>

17:02.855 --> 17:05.774
<i>It's Smoking Joe.</i>

17:08.277 --> 17:09.236
<i>I have no choice.</i>

17:09.862 --> 17:13.782
<i>The secret attack I intended to hold back
for a more difficult fight,</i>

17:14.366 --> 17:15.617
<i>I must now</i>

17:17.536 --> 17:19.038
<i>release it!</i>

17:23.542 --> 17:25.794
<i>Go forward.</i>

17:25.878 --> 17:27.046
<i>Even just a little bit.</i>

17:31.842 --> 17:33.052
<i>The philtrum.</i>

17:33.802 --> 17:36.055
<i>When struck directly by a fist,</i>

17:36.805 --> 17:40.601
<i>it is a tender area, as it serves
as a junction of facial nerves.</i>

17:40.684 --> 17:41.977
<i>A surefire vital spot.</i>

17:42.478 --> 17:45.522
<i>A spot that can leave
the victim comatose or even dead.</i>

17:45.606 --> 17:50.027
<i>It can paralyze all four limbs
and cease all movement.</i>

18:09.004 --> 18:10.589
Seriously?!

18:12.049 --> 18:14.593
You won! Yes!

18:16.303 --> 18:17.679
How mysterious...

18:18.180 --> 18:21.934
Awesome! You're so damn awesome!

18:22.017 --> 18:24.728
You defeated a real heavyweight!

18:27.022 --> 18:30.109
I saw my dead dad
for the first time in a long time.

18:31.110 --> 18:34.279
We were enjoying our long chat,
and the match had ended.

18:35.989 --> 18:39.618
It's thanks to you that I was able
to have a long talk with him.

18:42.371 --> 18:44.748
<i>Smoking Joe, you're wrong.</i>

18:45.582 --> 18:47.126
<i>You're not the loser.</i>

18:48.168 --> 18:51.130
<i>That move that I used, it's...</i>

18:57.219 --> 18:58.512
It's the champ!

18:58.595 --> 18:59.596
It's Bolt!

18:59.680 --> 19:00.556
Champ!

19:01.056 --> 19:04.143
The champ is congratulating Retsu!

19:04.226 --> 19:07.146
<i>This man is number one
in the boxing world.</i>

19:07.980 --> 19:09.898
<i>At the top of this world.</i>

19:14.695 --> 19:16.780
Thanks for what you did, Chiharu.

19:16.864 --> 19:18.031
Naw.

19:18.115 --> 19:21.994
Not only did I not win,
I couldn't even fight back.

19:22.744 --> 19:25.622
It was a cycle of getting beaten
then challenging him again.

19:25.706 --> 19:27.833
We fought a total of four times.

19:28.542 --> 19:31.712
I didn't have
a chance in a million of winning.

19:32.462 --> 19:33.881
You couldn't even touch him?

19:34.381 --> 19:38.302
No, he let me have quite a few punches.

19:39.011 --> 19:42.306
Especially the third time,
I got in some good ones.

19:42.890 --> 19:44.808
Then you did fight back.

19:44.892 --> 19:49.479
Naw, that was, y'know, special.

19:49.563 --> 19:50.689
It was just luck.

19:50.772 --> 19:52.774
It counts even if he was caught off guard.

19:52.858 --> 19:53.817
You think so?

19:54.943 --> 19:57.196
So, how did you lose?

19:59.907 --> 20:01.575
ICE PACK

20:29.186 --> 20:31.605
Eyes? His eyes?

20:31.688 --> 20:33.565
Yes, his eyes.

20:34.316 --> 20:37.361
I had my two fingers out like this,

20:37.444 --> 20:40.614
<i>and he rammed into them with his eyeballs.</i>

20:41.990 --> 20:43.617
Maybe it wasn't his eyes?

20:43.700 --> 20:45.619
No, it was his eyes.

20:45.702 --> 20:50.123
Chiharu, could you do the same thing?

20:52.626 --> 20:53.669
No, I couldn't.

20:54.836 --> 20:55.712
Why?

20:55.796 --> 20:59.258
What? My eyes would get crushed!

21:00.259 --> 21:02.386
You're afraid of losing your sight?

21:03.345 --> 21:07.391
To be honest, it'd be rough.
I couldn't blind myself willingly.

21:13.021 --> 21:15.148
So, something that Chiharu Shiba can't do,

21:15.691 --> 21:17.901
Baki Hanma managed to.

21:19.987 --> 21:24.408
So, I'm not saying this
'cause I'm sore about losing.

21:25.075 --> 21:29.746
But it seems to me that when he did that,

21:29.830 --> 21:32.666
he knew that his eyes wouldn't be crushed.

21:33.292 --> 21:35.419
At least, I think so.

21:35.502 --> 21:40.007
Fingers jamming into the eyes
wouldn't crush them?

21:41.967 --> 21:46.430
I mean, what if you went
at a totally superfast speed

21:46.513 --> 21:50.684
and totally rammed your eyes
right into somebody's fingers?

21:50.767 --> 21:53.437
If it was just fingers, then, y'know...

21:57.149 --> 22:00.444
I think it just might work.

22:02.070 --> 22:04.531
And what kind of speed was it?

22:08.785 --> 22:10.954
As fast as a bullet train, maybe?

22:12.080 --> 22:14.041
A bullet train?

22:15.125 --> 22:18.795
<i>I can't believe he believes me.</i>
